=== ENVIRONMENT — iOS-Simulator UI-exec blocker (evidence) ===
This is a NON-sandboxed host shared with sibling parallel slots. Throughout the
run the system was catastrophically oversubscribed:
    load averages sampled: 128, 511, 241, 266, 314, 573  on 20 cores
    (~23–28 concurrent xcodebuild/gradle/clang/swift-frontend processes)
Under that saturation the iOS-Simulator runtime services repeatedly died, so the
XCUITest *runner* could not bootstrap (this is infrastructure, not assertions):
    • "Early unexpected exit ... never finished bootstrapping — Test crashed with
       signal term/kill before establishing connection"
    • "Mach error -308 (ipc/mig) server died — Failed to install or launch the
       test runner"
    • "Setting up automation session" stretching to 20–25s then watchdog-restart
    • secondary: xcodebuild's diagnostic `xcrun simctl` losing DEVELOPER_DIR
Mitigations applied (pre-boot by UDID, fresh sim reboots, -parallel-testing-enabled
NO, -test-timeouts-enabled NO, single-suite/single-test scoping) did not overcome
a load of 130–573. The same instability fails the PRE-EXISTING UI tests too, and
even truncated a unit re-run — i.e. it is host-wide, not specific to the new code.
PROOF the new tests are sound where the host allowed a launch: the shell Dynamic-
Type case passed, and the 255-unit suite passed cleanly on this host.

=== CODE-DESIGN ISSUE FOUND + FIXED (no red-as-green) ===
First UI attempt that DID launch revealed a real defect: a plain SwiftUI VStack's
.accessibilityIdentifier is NOT surfaced as an XCUITest-queryable element (while a
ContentUnavailableView's IS — shell.pagePending.* worked, gallery.section.* did
not). Fixed: gallery container markers now use .accessibilityElement(children:
.contain)+.accessibilityIdentifier (helper `galleryMarker`), the documented way to
make a container addressable while keeping children individually accessible/
interactive; buttons + ContentUnavailableView markers stay plain. Recompiled green
(BFT=0) and re-passed all host gates. Full re-execution is deferred to a non-
saturated runner (same path as the macOS verification).

